\]
and \(P_t=0\) afterward. For every finite \(h\), conditioning on \(P_1=x_n\) with \(2^n+1>h\) gives \(\tau_1(1/2)=2^n+1\) with probability \(1\), hence \(\beta(h)=1\). But
